cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the modular noise simulator (src/noise_module) in published work,
  please cite it using the metadata below.
title: "Modular noise simulator: validated stationary, non-stationary, artifact and correlated multi-channel noise generation"
abstract: >-
  A composable noise simulation stack for detector-physics waveform studies. It
  provides a PSD-based stationary Gaussian single-channel core; correlated
  multi-channel generation in independent, shared-private and low-rank latent
  modes that returns both the implied and the realized covariance; temporal
  wrappers for non-stationarity, piecewise stationarity and drift; injection of
  spectral lines, glitches and bursts; PSD resampling between sampling rates;
  and a confidence-aware validation suite with bootstrap intervals over
  cross-spectral-density ensembles. It was written to provide a controlled
  testbed in which the assumed and the realized noise covariance are both known.
type: software
